%% Figure 5: Runtime Configuration and Secrets Ingestion via AWS SSM Parameter Store
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Host as EC2 Host (Systemd Bootstrap)
    participant Script as refresh-env.sh (boto3 client)
    participant IMDS as EC2 Metadata Service (IMDSv2)
    participant IAM as AWS IAM (finance-tracker-ec2-role)
    participant SSM as AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store
    participant KMS as AWS KMS (alias/aws/ssm)
    participant Env as Host File (/opt/finance-tracker/.env)
    participant Docker as Docker Container (finance-tracker-app)

    Host->>Script: Execute sudo /opt/finance-tracker/refresh-env.sh
    Script->>IMDS: PUT /latest/api/token (TTL: 21600s)
    IMDS-->>Script: Return IMDSv2 Session Token
    Script->>IMDS: GET /latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/finance-tracker-ec2-role
    IMDS-->>Script: Temporary STS AccessKey, SecretKey, Token

    Script->>SSM: GetParametersByPath(Path="/finance-tracker/", WithDecryption=True)
    Note over SSM: IAM Policy check: parameter/finance-tracker/*
    SSM->>KMS: Decrypt SecureString parameters (DB_PASSWORD, SECRET_KEY, MAIL_PASSWORD)
    KMS-->>SSM: Return Decrypted Plaintext Values
    SSM-->>Script: 14 Key-Value Parameters Dictionary

    Note over Script: Validate 14 required keys non-empty<br/>Serialize Compose-safe values to .env.tmp
    Script->>Env: chmod 600 + os.replace(/opt/finance-tracker/.env)
    
    Host->>Docker: systemctl restart finance-tracker.service (docker compose up -d)
    Docker->>Env: Read .env (restricted permissions rw-------)
    Note over Docker: Flask initialize DB engine & Gunicorn workers start
